    <DataNode elementId="AT1G05630-MONOMER" textLabel="Type I inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase 13" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9SYK4" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="495" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">5PTase13 has |FRAME: MG+2 Mg&lt;SUP&gt;2+&lt;/SUP&gt;|-dependent inositol polyphosphate 5-phosphatase activity against |FRAME: INOSITOL-1-4-5-TRISPHOSPHATE D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol (1,4,5)-trisphosphate| when its activity is tested &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; following expression in yeast. In the same assays, it shows no activity against the membrane-based phosphoinositides (|FRAME: CPD-177 a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3-phosphate|, |FRAME: CPD-1108 a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol 4-phosphate|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-5-PHOSPHA a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 5-phosphate|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-34-BISPH a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,4-bisphosphate|, |FRAME: 1-PHOSPHATIDYL-1D-MYO-INOSITOL-35-BISPH 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,5-bisphosphate|, |FRAME: |, |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYL-MYO-INOSITOL-45-BISPHOSPHA a 1-phosphatidyl-1D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol 4,5-bisphosphate| or |FRAME: PHOSPHATIDYLINOSITOL-345-TRIPHOSPHATE 1-phosphatidyl-1D-myo-inositol 3,4,5-trisphosphate|), nor does it show any activity with the soluble tetraphosphate inositol |FRAME: CPD-506 D-&lt;i&gt;myo&lt;/i&gt;-inositol (1,3,4,5)-tetrakisphosphate| |CITS: [15574849]|. Interestingly, in addition to its type II 5PTase domain, this enzyme also has a WD40 protein-protein interaction domain |CITS: [15574849]| and it has been shown to physically interact with protein kinase SnRK1 |CITS: [18931139]| thus giving it the potential to influence sugar signaling. 5PTase13 transcripts appear to be expressed at higher levels in seedlings, young stems, and shoot apices than in other organs. In addition, 5PTase13 transcript expression levels appear to increase in response to ABA and wounding stress |CITS: [15574849]|. A 5PTase13:GFP fusion protein localizes to the nucleus |CITS: [18931139]|. &lt;i&gt;5ptase13-1&lt;/i&gt; mutants have aberrant cotyledon vein patterning |CITS: [16299182 ]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G05630-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G05630.1" />
